@@ -236,3 +236,11 @@ In **Admin → Appointments**, choose **Edit ticket** to correct the customer's
 Changing a contact phone does not change the customer's portal username or assign the ticket to another account. A changed number clears appointment SMS consent until the customer opts in again. Saving a ticket edit does not send a new email or text; pending messages with superseded contact, device, service, name, or price details are stopped. The editor rejects stale changes so a second browser cannot silently overwrite a newer edit.
 
 **Delete ticket** opens a separate review and requires the exact displayed numeric ticket number. Deletion permanently removes that appointment, its before/after photos, checkout record, saved condition answers, queued notification records, and ticket-specific access challenges. Customer accounts, other tickets, employees, time records, and the ticket-number sequence remain. Deleted ticket links and photo links no longer open the record. An edit or deletion is temporarily blocked while an appointment message is processing; refresh and retry after it finishes.
+
+## AI receptionist integration
+
+The separate AI receptionist uses `/api/integrations/receptionist/v1/`. Configure a dedicated random `RECEPTIONIST_API_TOKEN` and the exact `RECEPTIONIST_ORIGIN`; use HTTPS except for loopback development. Its staff authorization flow reuses your existing admin/employee login, requires explicit approval and PKCE, and issues short-lived grants. Revoked/expired staff sessions are rejected on subsequent operations. For this integration, employees are restricted to their assigned locations; administrators can access all stores.
+
+Customers must verify a code delivered to the ticket's registered contact before reading its status. Caller ID alone grants no access. Missing message-provider configuration does not bypass verification. Customer-visible projections omit internal notes and account credentials.
+
+Bookings use the original availability/intake/notification workflow with transaction-scoped idempotency hooks. Confirmed cancellations require a staff grant and the exact current ticket version; their audit and notification records commit with the change. Intake and checkout prerequisites remain mandatory; there is no unrestricted status setter. Apply `20261023010000_receptionist_integration` with your normal migration process before enabling this API. No production migration or deployment was performed during local development.
